>
  <p>
    Hurricane has its own city code, Building Department, and utility service, and its fence rules differ from St. George's in
    ways that matter: the front-yard limit is stated as 48 inches for opaque fences, the side and rear limit is 6 feet rather
    than St. George's 6 feet 4 inches, and utility easements are off limits. This page summarizes Hurricane City Code §10-37-9,
    read on September 26, 2026.
  </p>

  <h2>Hurricane fence and wall rules at a glance</h2>
  <IconList items={rules} />

  <h2>Easements come first</h2>
  <p>
    If your lot has a public utility easement (your plat shows it), the Building Department states plainly that no structures of
    any kind are permitted within it, regardless of zoning. Before a fence or wall line is set, find any easements on your plat
    and keep posts and footings out of them. Call 811 (<a href="https://www.bluestakes.org/" rel="noopener">Blue Stakes of Utah</a>) at least 3 business days before digging.
  </p>

  <h2>Pools</h2>
  <p>
    §10-37-9(D) requires permanent swimming pools that are not inside a building to be completely surrounded by a fence or wall
    that satisfies building code requirements. The section does not restate those requirements, so ask the Building Department
    what applies to your pool before you choose a fence. Our <a href="/pool-fence-and-gate-st-george-ut/">pool fence guide</a>
    lists the questions to ask.
  </p>

  <h2>Footings, frost, and wind</h2>
  <p>
    Hurricane's Building Department lists its design criteria, including a 12-inch frost line depth and a 105 mph design wind
    speed. Those figures are written for buildings, but they are good prompts for a fence or wall quote: ask how deep posts and
    footings will go, and how a tall solid fence or block wall is designed to handle wind.
  </p>

  <h2>What it costs</h2>
  <p>
    No Hurricane fence or wall company publishes prices. As of {COST_AS_OF}, typical residential fence projects in the St. George
    area run about {fenceProject.low}–{fenceProject.high} installed, and CMU block walls about {blockWall.perSqFt} per square foot. See
    the <a href="/fence-and-block-wall-cost-st-george-ut/">cost guide</a> for every range and source.
  </p>

